<article class="env-lemma" id="0893">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0893">Lemma <span data-tag="0893">29.38.9</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes. Let $\mathcal{L}$ be an invertible $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. Let $S' \to S$ be a morphism of schemes. Let $f' : X' \to S'$ be the base change of $f$ and denote $\mathcal{L}'$ the pullback of $\mathcal{L}$ to $X'$. If $\mathcal{L}$ is $f$-ample, then $\mathcal{L}'$ is $f'$-ample. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/01VJ" data-tag="01VJ">29.38.4</a> it suffices to find an affine open covering $S' = \bigcup U'_ i$ such that $\mathcal{L}'$ restricts to an ample invertible sheaf on $(f')^{-1}(U_ i')$ for all $i$. We may choose $U'_ i$ mapping into an affine open $U_ i \subset S$. In this case the morphism $(f')^{-1}(U'_ i) \to f^{-1}(U_ i)$ is affine as a base change of the affine morphism $U'_ i \to U_ i$ (Lemma <a href="/tag/01SD" data-tag="01SD">29.11.9</a>). Thus $\mathcal{L}'|_{(f')^{-1}(U'_ i)}$ is ample by Lemma <a href="/tag/0892" data-tag="0892">29.38.7</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>